    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-5> ;
    schema:about "Arabidopsis thaliana (shoot apical meristem L1 epidermal shell, organ-meristem saddle boundary, cylindrical stem, and epidermal cells)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A 3D curved-surface vertex or FEM shell solver, the Bozorg (2014) stress-vs-strain discrimination as an emergent property of the mesh (both cues give circumferential CMTs around the wound here), auxin-maximum (phyllotactic) patterning from PIN1 up-the-gradient transport, subcellular katanin dynamics, or internal L2/L3 corpus mechanics",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Section 2: 4-zone pressurized-shell stress table (prescribed sigma_1, sigma_2 per zone), nematic CMT order S = gamma a / (gamma a + 2 D_theta), stiffness anisotropy and viscoplastic Lockhart strain rates; exact integer checks of Lean Laws 1-3; an analytic (Gaussian-weight) 2D cross-section anisotropy field labelled 'FEM' in v2",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Section 3: 24-cell ring with prescribed angular dispersions for stress / strain / bot1 cues; closed-form 5-condition sweep of S, crease depth and ablation cos^2 fitted to the reference JSON (Pearson r = 0.9992 against the same JSON)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Section 3b (Pass 3): 2D L1 cellular vertex mesh — zone stress tensor as affine boundary pre-strain epsilon_i = sigma_i / E_shell; Hookean wall tensions; virial wall-stress tensor and wall-strain tensor per cell; CMT director relaxation with gamma_MT and S; cellulose reinforcement of CMT-parallel walls; softmax PIN1 allocation on wall tension; PIN1-polar auxin transport with diffusion, production and decay; auxin-enhanced Lockhart creep; division along sigma_1 (else Errera); T1 detection and flip (disabled by default); 9 scenarios with emergent PIN1/CMT co-alignment 0.747 (saddle WT), wound-ring CMT circumferential cos^2 0.985, PIN1 away-from-wound fraction 0.83 in WT and 0.83 under oryzalin, katanin sweep r = 0.995, 57 divisions with Euler residual 0",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Section 4: optical-density segmentation and Sobel/Gaussian structure-tensor coherency on the SHA-256-locked longitudinal SAM section (dome / saddle / stem ROIs)",
        "reported_in_source: Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 and Bozorg, Krupinski & Jönsson (2014) PLoS Comput. Biol. 10:e1003410: pressurized-shell / finite-element stress models of the SAM with isotropic stress on the central dome (K > 0), anisotropic tensile stress along the negative-Gaussian-curvature organ boundary (K < 0), 2:1 hoop-to-axial Laplace stress on the stem, circumferential CMTs around single-cell ablations, and the argument that maximal principal stress, not strain, is the directional cue",
        "reported_in_source: Heisler et al. (2010) PLoS Biol. 8:e1000516: PIN1 polarity correlates with CMT orientation (PIN1-rich membranes parallel to the CMT array), both reorient after ablation (CMTs circumferential, PIN1 directed away from the wound) and the PIN1 response persists under oryzalin; hypothesis that PIN1 accumulates at the most stressed anticlinal wall",
        "reported_in_source: Louveaux et al. (2016) PNAS 113:E4294-E4303: SAM cells, especially at the organ boundary, orient division planes along maximal tensile stress, deviating from the Errera shortest-wall rule when stress is anisotropic",
        "reported_in_source: Uyttewaal et al. (2012) Cell 149:439-451 and Sampathkumar et al. (2014) eLife 3:e01967: katanin (BOT1/KTN1) sets the mechanical feedback gain; bot1/ktn1 and oryzalin reduce CMT ordering and flatten the boundary crease",
        "transfer_boundary: The Heisler (2010) and Louveaux (2016) reference values used for the new measurements are within-30-degree ordinal thresholds (cos^2 >= 0.75) derived from the papers' qualitative statements, with 0.5 as the random null; no figure of either paper was digitised",
        "transfer_boundary: The specimen is a stained longitudinal histological section, not an apical PIN1-GFP / MBD-GFP image, so its structure-tensor coherency measures cell-wall edge anisotropy in the section plane, not CMT or PIN1 organisation",
        "transfer_boundary: The vertex mesh is a tangent-plane (2D) approximation of the L1 sheet: curvature enters only through the boundary pre-strain, so dome vs saddle differ by boundary anisotropy, not by Gaussian curvature of a 3D surface; absolute S values on the mesh (dome 0.42, saddle 0.57, stem 0.59) are compared with but do not match the Hamant 2008 zone references (0.08, 0.81, 0.57)" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Auxin flux vein / phyllotactic primordium in Arabidopsis thaliana" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "4. Polar Auxin & Turgor Stress" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Spirals, Veins & Puzzle Cells" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Golden Angle / Auxin Flux" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Arabidopsis" ;
