<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008), Bozorg et al. (2014), Sampathkumar et al. (2014), Uyttewaal et al. (2012), Heisler et al. (2010) & Louveaux et al. (2016) shoot apical meristem shell stress tensor, stress-vs-strain CMT alignment, katanin boundary morphogenesis and PIN1/CMT co-alignment on a growing L1 cellular vertex mesh — Code-to-model traceability: 76/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the module docstring (L1-86) maps Laws 1-5 to equations, papers and Lean theorem line ranges and names the implementing functions; `simulate_l1_vertex_patch` carries an explicit coupling-chain docstring (L1034-1044) and each mesh method states its source rule (Batchelor virial, Heisler softmax, Louveaux division, Hamant & Traas on T1); the honest-scope note names the 2D reduction and the phenomenological sections. Deductions: the sweep constants 1.45, 0.68, 0.806, 15.95, 13.45 (L413-416) and the ring dispersions 0.245 / 0.62 / 0.81 (L391-394) have no citation (-8); `build_2d_meristem_fem_field` is still named and titled 'FEM' in Panel A although the docstring now says it is analytic (-6); the mesh constants (k_wall = 6, K_A = 0.9, beta_pin = 4, phi_wall = 0.45, E_shell = 400 MPa) are documented in the JSON but not derived from any paper value (-6); the softmax PIN1 rule is a modelling choice attributed to Heisler's hypothesis rather than an equation in the paper (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L413–L416: Uncited fitted exponents and offsets in the 5-condition sweep <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L413-L416>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008), Bozorg et al. (2014), Sampathkumar et al. (2014), Uyttewaal et al. (2012), Heisler et al. (2010) & Louveaux et al. (2016) shoot apical meristem shell stress tensor, stress-vs-strain CMT alignment, katanin boundary morphogenesis and PIN1/CMT co-alignment on a growing L1 cellular vertex mesh — Model fidelity to source: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the vertex mesh implements recognisable published mechanisms — Hookean anticlinal wall tension with Lockhart creep above a yield strain (`wall_state` L674-682, `step_fields` L819-835), the Batchelor virial wall-stress tensor sum_e T_e l_e t⊗t and its principal axis as the CMT cue (`cell_tensors` L722-747), nematic S = gamma a / (gamma a + 2 D_theta) in the Bozorg Eq. 12 form (L790-798), cellulose reinforcement of CMT-parallel walls closing the stress feedback loop (`_wall_stiffness` L665-672), Heisler's stress-based PIN1 rule as a softmax on wall tension with PIN1-polar auxin fluxes (`pin1_state` L749-770, transport L803-817), division along sigma_1 with an Errera fallback (L1062-1093) and a correct, unit-tested T1 flip (`apply_t1` L922-965); Laws 4-5 are machine-checked. Deductions: the mesh is 2D, so the saddle's negative Gaussian curvature is replaced by an anisotropic boundary pre-strain (L1046-1047) — the K < 0 vs K > 0 physics of Law 1 is not on the mesh (-8); the v2 'FEM' field is a sum of hand-placed Gaussians (L325-330) and the per-zone principal stresses are prescribed constants (L173-215), not solved from turgor and curvature (-8); the 5-condition sweep is a closed-form fit with uncited exponents 1.45 / 0.68 / 15.95 and literal strain-cue and oryzalin values (L412-432) (-6); the Bozorg stress-vs-strain discrimination does not emerge on the mesh (ablation CMT circumferential 0.985 vs 0.968 for the strain cue; L1137-1155 report it) (-4); auxin feedback on growth is phenomenological (k_aux on creep) and no auxin maximum forms (-2); in-plane turgor is a small residual (P = 0.15) with periclinal area elasticity standing in for the out-of-plane pressure load (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L173–L215: Per-zone sigma_1 / sigma_2 are prescribed multiples of sigma_0 (e.g. 1.90, 0.30) rather than solved from curvature and turgor <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L173-L215>",
        "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L325–L330: '2D FEM' anisotropy field is three hand-placed Gaussian weights plus a lateral_compression constant — not a finite-element solve <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L325-L330>",
        "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L412–L432: 5-condition sweep: closed-form S_pred / depth with uncited constants; strain-cue and oryzalin S, depth, cos^2 and r are literals <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L412-L432>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008), Bozorg et al. (2014), Sampathkumar et al. (2014), Uyttewaal et al. (2012), Heisler et al. (2010) & Louveaux et al. (2016) shoot apical meristem shell stress tensor, stress-vs-strain CMT alignment, katanin boundary morphogenesis and PIN1/CMT co-alignment on a growing L1 cellular vertex mesh — Morphometric validation: 60/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: `measure_morphoeval` (L1344-1519) now returns 16 measurements; the 7 Pass 3 entries (L1451-1518) are emergent quantities computed on the mesh — PIN1-wall/CMT co-alignment with bot1 and oryzalin controls, PIN1 away-from-wound fraction WT vs oryzalin, wound-ring CMT cos^2 with the oryzalin null, division-plane alignment with the Errera-only counterfactual (1.00 vs 0.18), Euler residual, the 3-point katanin sweep r and the zone-S RMSE (0.24, which exposes the dome over-prediction rather than hiding it) — each with a stated method, a reference and a random null. Deductions: the legacy 'Bozorg stress cue vs strain-cue correlation r = 0.991 / -0.415' (L1397-1405) is a literal constant copied from the reference JSON at L420 and L426 and reported as a measurement with reference 0.991 — circular (-12); the 5-condition depth Pearson r = 0.9992 (L1424-1432) correlates closed-form fits against the very JSON they were fitted to (-8); two specimen measurements set reference_value equal to the measured value (L1438, L1447) (-4); the new Heisler / Louveaux references are ordinal 0.75 thresholds, not digitised figure values, and the WT co-alignment (0.747) sits just under that threshold (-6); the vertex-mesh S values differ from the zone references by up to 0.34 (dome) (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L1397–L1405: 'Principal stress cue r = 0.991 vs strain-cue r = -0.415' measurement is the literal emp_r constant from L420/L426, not a computed correlation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L1397-L1405>",
        "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L1424–L1432: 5-condition Pearson r compares fitted closed forms with the reference JSON they were fitted to <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L1424-L1432>",
        "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L1438–L1447: Specimen coherency and area-fraction measurements use reference_value = value (self-referential) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L1438-L1447>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-5-condition-perturbation-morphospace-boundary-depth-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-arabidopsis-sam-specimen-saddle-boundary-vs-central-dome-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-arabidopsis-sam-specimen-segmented-tissue-area-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-bozorg-et-al-2014-principal-stress-cue-vs-strain-cue-control-alignment-correlation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-euler-characteristic-residual-chi-after-chi-before-over-all-vertex-mesh-topological-events-divisions-t1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-heisler-2010-fraction-of-wound-ring-cells-with-pin1-polarity-directed-away-from-the-ablated-cell-wt-vs-oryzalin>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-heisler-2010-pin1-rich-wall-axis-vs-cmt-director-co-alignment-cos-2-on-the-growing-saddle-boundary-l1-vertex-mesh-wt>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-law-1-saddle-boundary-stress-amplification-algebraic-residual>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-law-2-law-3-cylinder-laplace-switch-and-katanin-oryzalin-stiffness-residual>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-louveaux-2016-division-plane-alignment-with-local-sigma-1-in-the-saddle-boundary-stress-rule-vs-errera-shortest-wall-prediction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-organ-meristem-saddle-boundary-k-0-vs-central-dome-k-0-cmt-nematic-order-s>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-single-cell-laser-ablation-ring-circumferential-cmt-alignment-cos-2-delta-theta>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-vertex-mesh-katanin-gain-sweep-saddle-cmt-order-s-at-gamma-mt-0-0-45-2-40-vs-reference-boundary-s-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-vertex-mesh-zone-cmt-order-s-dome-saddle-stem-rmse-vs-hamant-2008-reference-s>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-wild-type-vs-bot1-ktn1-katanin-mutant-and-oryzalin-ablation-boundary-crease-depth>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-measurement-wound-ring-cmt-circumferential-alignment-cos-2-emerging-on-the-vertex-mesh-wt-stress-cue-vs-oryzalin>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

