<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008) & Bozorg et al. (2014) Saddle-Boundary Stress Anisotropy Amplification & Gaussian Curvature Inversion Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that transitioning from the positive-Gaussian-curvature SAM dome (K > 0) to the negative-Gaussian-curvature organ boundary saddle (K < 0) switches tensile stress from isotropic (Δσ = 0) to strongly amplified along the boundary crease axis | Variables: κ_1, κ_2: principal curvatures along and across organ-meristem boundary (μm^-1); K = κ_1 κ_2: Gaussian curvature (μm^-2); P_s: turgor shell stress scale; Δσ: principal tensile stress difference (MPa)" ;
    dct:source "Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 Fig. 2 & SOM; Bozorg et al. (2014) PLoS Comput. Biol. 10(1):e1003410 Figs. 3-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L147-L286>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean#L30-L65> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gaussian_curvature (kappa_1 kappa_2 : Int) : Int :=
  kappa_1 * kappa_2
def saddle_stress_anisotropy (P_s kappa_1 kappa_2 : Int) : Int :=
  P_s * (kappa_1 - kappa_2)
theorem hamant_bozorg_saddle_boundary_stress_anisotropy_amplification
    (P_s kappa_0 kappa_s : Int)
    (hP : P_s > 0) (hk0 : kappa_0 > 0) (hks : kappa_s > 0) :
    gaussian_curvature kappa_0 kappa_0 > 0 ∧
    saddle_stress_anisotropy P_s kappa_0 kappa_0 = 0 ∧
    gaussian_curvature kappa_0 (-kappa_s) < 0 ∧
    saddle_stress_anisotropy P_s kappa_0 (-kappa_s) = P_s * kappa_0 + P_s * kappa_s ∧
    saddle_stress_anisotropy P_s kappa_0 (-kappa_s) > P_s * kappa_0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "K = κ_1 κ_2;  Δσ(P_s, κ_1, κ_2) = P_s (κ_1 - κ_2);  Δσ(P_s, κ_0, κ_0) = 0 (dome, K > 0) vs Δσ(P_s, κ_0, -κ_s) = P_s(κ_0 + κ_s) > P_s κ_0 > 0 (saddle crease, K < 0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.048>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8137.2009.03100.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Finite-Element Pressurized Shell Turgor Stress Tensor, Bozorg Stress-vs-Strain Cue Discrimination, Anisotropic Viscoplastic Lockhart Growth & (Pass 3) Heisler PIN1/CMT Co-Alignment on a Growing L1 Cellular Vertex Mesh" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.saddle_stress_anisotropy" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.hamant_bozorg_saddle_boundary_stress_anisotropy_amplification" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Bozorg et al. (2014) & Hamant et al. (2008) Cylindrical Stem 2:1 Hoop-to-Axial Laplace Stress Switch & Longitudinal Lockhart Elongation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that the 2:1 circumferential-to-axial Laplace stress ratio on the cylindrical stem drives transverse cortical microtubule hoops and longitudinal stem elongation when transverse cellulose reinforcement reduces circumferential compliance below C_z / 2 | Variables: S_0 = P R / (2 h): axial Laplace stress (MPa); σ_θ = 2 S_0: circumferential hoop stress (MPa); C_z, C_θ: axial and circumferential viscoplastic compliances (MPa^-1 hr^-1)" ;
    dct:source "Bozorg et al. (2014) PLoS Comput. Biol. 10(1):e1003410 Fig. 2; Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 Fig. 1" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L147-L286>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean#L81-L115> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cylinder_axial_stress (S_0 : Int) : Int := S_0
def cylinder_hoop_stress (S_0 : Int) : Int := 2 * S_0
def lockhart_elongation_rate (compliance sigma : Int) : Int := compliance * sigma
theorem bozorg_cylinder_to_saddle_stress_switch
    (S_0 C_z C_theta : Int)
    (hS : S_0 > 0) (hC : C_z > 2 * C_theta) :
    cylinder_hoop_stress S_0 = 2 * cylinder_axial_stress S_0 ∧
    cylinder_hoop_stress S_0 - cylinder_axial_stress S_0 = S_0 ∧
    cylinder_hoop_stress S_0 > cylinder_axial_stress S_0 ∧
    lockhart_elongation_rate C_z (cylinder_axial_stress S_0) -
      lockhart_elongation_rate C_theta (cylinder_hoop_stress S_0) =
      (C_z - 2 * C_theta) * S_0 ∧
    lockhart_elongation_rate C_z (cylinder_axial_stress S_0) >
      lockhart_elongation_rate C_theta (cylinder_hoop_stress S_0)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "σ_θ = P R / h = 2 S_0 = 2 σ_z > σ_z;  ε̇_z - ε̇_θ = C_z σ_z - C_θ σ_θ = (C_z - 2 C_θ) S_0 > 0  for C_z > 2 C_θ" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.048>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8137.2009.03100.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Finite-Element Pressurized Shell Turgor Stress Tensor, Bozorg Stress-vs-Strain Cue Discrimination, Anisotropic Viscoplastic Lockhart Growth & (Pass 3) Heisler PIN1/CMT Co-Alignment on a Growing L1 Cellular Vertex Mesh" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.cylinder_hoop_stress" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.bozorg_cylinder_to_saddle_stress_switch" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Uyttewaal et al. (2012) & Hamant et al. (2008) Katanin (bot1/KTN1) & Oryzalin Mechanical Feedback Gain Reduction Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that reducing mechanical stress feedback gain γ_MT via katanin (bot1/ktn1) loss-of-function or Oryzalin microtubule depolymerization (γ_MT = 0) reduces or abolishes cellulose stiffness anisotropy and organ-meristem boundary crease folding | Variables: γ_MT: katanin-dependent mechanical stress feedback gain; E_1, E_2: principal cell-wall elastic moduli along and perpendicular to maximal stress (MPa); Δσ: principal stress difference (MPa)" ;
    dct:source "Uyttewaal et al. (2012) Cell 149:439-451 Figs. 2-5; Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 Fig. 5" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L357-L480>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean#L132-L167> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def wall_modulus_max (E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_MT : Int) : Int :=
  E_0 + dE * Delta_sigma * gamma_MT
def wall_modulus_min (E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_MT : Int) : Int :=
  E_0 - dE * Delta_sigma * gamma_MT
def wall_stiffness_anisotropy (E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_MT : Int) : Int :=
  wall_modulus_max E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_MT - wall_modulus_min E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_MT
theorem uyttewaal_katanin_oryzalin_feedback_gain_reduction
    (E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_WT gamma_bot1 : Int)
    (hdE : dE > 0) (hDS : Delta_sigma > 0) (hG : gamma_WT > gamma_bot1) :
    wall_stiffness_anisotropy E_0 dE Delta_sigma 0 = 0 ∧
    wall_stiffness_anisotropy E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_WT -
      wall_stiffness_anisotropy E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_bot1 =
      2 * (dE * Delta_sigma * (gamma_WT - gamma_bot1)) ∧
    wall_stiffness_anisotropy E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_WT >
      wall_stiffness_anisotropy E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_bot1
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "ΔE(γ_MT) = E_1(γ_MT) - E_2(γ_MT) = 2 dE Δσ γ_MT;  ΔE(0) = 0 (Oryzalin);  ΔE(γ_WT) - ΔE(γ_bot1) = 2 dE Δσ (γ_WT - γ_bot1) > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.048>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8137.2009.03100.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Finite-Element Pressurized Shell Turgor Stress Tensor, Bozorg Stress-vs-Strain Cue Discrimination, Anisotropic Viscoplastic Lockhart Growth & (Pass 3) Heisler PIN1/CMT Co-Alignment on a Growing L1 Cellular Vertex Mesh" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.wall_stiffness_anisotropy" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.uyttewaal_katanin_oryzalin_feedback_gain_reduction" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Heisler et al. (2010) Stress-Based PIN1 Polarity / CMT Co-Alignment & Microtubule-Independence Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that PIN1 allocated to the most-tensed wall and CMTs aligned with the virial σ_1 axis pick the same wall axis (co-alignment), that this holds without microtubules (γ_MT = 0, oryzalin) and is only amplified by wild-type katanin feedback | Variables: a: cell side (μm); T_0: isotropic anticlinal wall tension; τ: tension increment on σ_1-parallel walls from the shell stress tensor; M_xx - M_yy: virial (Batchelor) wall-stress anisotropy Σ_e T_e l_e t_e⊗t_e; κ S γ_MT: katanin/cellulose reinforcement of CMT-parallel walls" ;
    dct:source "Heisler et al. (2010) PLoS Biol. 8(10):e1000516 Figs. 2-6; Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 Fig. 3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L509-L1156>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean#L165-L226> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def wall_tension_parallel (T_0 tau : Int) : Int := T_0 + tau
def wall_tension_perpendicular (T_0 : Int) : Int := T_0
def virial_stress_anisotropy (a T_par T_perp : Int) : Int := 2 * a * T_par - 2 * a * T_perp
def cmt_reinforced_parallel_tension (T_0 tau kappa S gamma_MT : Int) : Int := T_0 + tau + kappa * S * gamma_MT
theorem heisler_pin1_cmt_coalignment_under_anisotropic_wall_tension
    (a T_0 tau kappa S gamma_MT : Int)
    (ha : a > 0) (_hT : T_0 > 0) (htau : tau > 0)
    (hkappa : kappa ≥ 0) (hS : S ≥ 0) (hgamma : gamma_MT ≥ 0) :
    wall_tension_parallel T_0 tau > wall_tension_perpendicular T_0 ∧
    virial_stress_anisotropy a (wall_tension_parallel T_0 tau) (wall_tension_perpendicular T_0) = 2 * a * tau ∧
    virial_stress_anisotropy a (wall_tension_parallel T_0 tau) (wall_tension_perpendicular T_0) > 0 ∧
    cmt_reinforced_parallel_tension T_0 tau kappa S 0 = wall_tension_parallel T_0 tau ∧
    cmt_reinforced_parallel_tension T_0 tau kappa S 0 > wall_tension_perpendicular T_0 ∧
    cmt_reinforced_parallel_tension T_0 tau kappa S gamma_MT ≥ wall_tension_parallel T_0 tau
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "T_∥ = T_0 + τ > T_⊥ = T_0;  M_xx - M_yy = 2 a T_∥ - 2 a T_⊥ = 2 a τ > 0 (σ_1 axis = PIN1-rich wall axis = CMT director);  T_∥(γ_MT) = T_0 + τ + κ S γ_MT with T_∥(0) = T_0 + τ > T_⊥ (oryzalin) and T_∥(γ_MT) ≥ T_∥(0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.048>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8137.2009.03100.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Finite-Element Pressurized Shell Turgor Stress Tensor, Bozorg Stress-vs-Strain Cue Discrimination, Anisotropic Viscoplastic Lockhart Growth & (Pass 3) Heisler PIN1/CMT Co-Alignment on a Growing L1 Cellular Vertex Mesh" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.virial_stress_anisotropy" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.heisler_pin1_cmt_coalignment_under_anisotropic_wall_tension" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Louveaux et al. (2016) & Hamant & Traas (2010) Vertex-Mesh Topological Event Law — Division Preserves the Euler Characteristic, T1 is Topology-Neutral (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Fixes the bookkeeping invariant that every division (two vertices inserted on existing walls, one new wall, one new cell) and every T1 flip must satisfy on the mesh; verified numerically after each event in simulate_l1_vertex_patch and verify_t1_transition_topology | Variables: V, E, F: vertices, walls and cells of the planar L1 vertex mesh (outer face excluded, χ = 1 for a disc); n: number of symmetric divisions" ;
    dct:source "Louveaux et al. (2016) PNAS 113(30):E4294-E4303 Figs. 2-4 (division along maximal tensile stress); Hamant & Traas (2010) New Phytol. 185:369-385 (no neighbour exchange in cemented plant tissue)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L874-L965>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean#L230-L268> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def euler_characteristic (V E F : Int) : Int := V - E + F
def vertices_after_divisions (V n : Int) : Int := V + 2 * n
def edges_after_divisions (E n : Int) : Int := E + 3 * n
def cells_after_divisions (F n : Int) : Int := F + n
theorem louveaux_vertex_mesh_division_preserves_euler_characteristic
    (V E F n : Int) (hn : n ≥ 0) :
    euler_characteristic (vertices_after_divisions V 1) (edges_after_divisions E 1) (cells_after_divisions F 1) = euler_characteristic V E F ∧
    cells_after_divisions F 1 > F ∧
    euler_characteristic (vertices_after_divisions V n) (edges_after_divisions E n) (cells_after_divisions F n) = euler_characteristic V E F ∧
    cells_after_divisions F n ≥ F ∧
    euler_characteristic V E F = euler_characteristic V E F
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "χ = V - E + F;  division along σ_1: (V, E, F) → (V + 2, E + 3, F + 1), χ invariant, F + 1 > F;  after n ≥ 0 divisions (V + 2n, E + 3n, F + n) has the same χ;  T1: (V, E, F) unchanged" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.048>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8137.2009.03100.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Finite-Element Pressurized Shell Turgor Stress Tensor, Bozorg Stress-vs-Strain Cue Discrimination, Anisotropic Viscoplastic Lockhart Growth & (Pass 3) Heisler PIN1/CMT Co-Alignment on a Growing L1 Cellular Vertex Mesh" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.euler_characteristic" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.louveaux_vertex_mesh_division_preserves_euler_characteristic" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008) & Bozorg et al. (2014) Saddle-Boundary Stress Anisotropy Amplification & Gaussian Curvature Inversion Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that transitioning from the positive-Gaussian-curvature SAM dome (K > 0) to the negative-Gaussian-curvature organ boundary saddle (K < 0) switches tensile stress from isotropic (Δσ = 0) to strongly amplified along the boundary crease axis | Variables: κ_1, κ_2: principal curvatures along and across organ-meristem boundary (μm^-1); K = κ_1 κ_2: Gaussian curvature (μm^-2); P_s: turgor shell stress scale; Δσ: principal tensile stress difference (MPa)" ;
    dct:source "Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 Fig. 2 & SOM; Bozorg et al. (2014) PLoS Comput. Biol. 10(1):e1003410 Figs. 3-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L147-L286>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean#L30-L65> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gaussian_curvature (kappa_1 kappa_2 : Int) : Int :=
  kappa_1 * kappa_2
def saddle_stress_anisotropy (P_s kappa_1 kappa_2 : Int) : Int :=
  P_s * (kappa_1 - kappa_2)
theorem hamant_bozorg_saddle_boundary_stress_anisotropy_amplification
    (P_s kappa_0 kappa_s : Int)
    (hP : P_s > 0) (hk0 : kappa_0 > 0) (hks : kappa_s > 0) :
    gaussian_curvature kappa_0 kappa_0 > 0 ∧
    saddle_stress_anisotropy P_s kappa_0 kappa_0 = 0 ∧
    gaussian_curvature kappa_0 (-kappa_s) < 0 ∧
    saddle_stress_anisotropy P_s kappa_0 (-kappa_s) = P_s * kappa_0 + P_s * kappa_s ∧
    saddle_stress_anisotropy P_s kappa_0 (-kappa_s) > P_s * kappa_0
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "K = κ_1 κ_2;  Δσ(P_s, κ_1, κ_2) = P_s (κ_1 - κ_2);  Δσ(P_s, κ_0, κ_0) = 0 (dome, K > 0) vs Δσ(P_s, κ_0, -κ_s) = P_s(κ_0 + κ_s) > P_s κ_0 > 0 (saddle crease, K < 0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.048>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8137.2009.03100.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Finite-Element Pressurized Shell Turgor Stress Tensor, Bozorg Stress-vs-Strain Cue Discrimination, Anisotropic Viscoplastic Lockhart Growth & (Pass 3) Heisler PIN1/CMT Co-Alignment on a Growing L1 Cellular Vertex Mesh" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.saddle_stress_anisotropy" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.hamant_bozorg_saddle_boundary_stress_anisotropy_amplification" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Bozorg et al. (2014) & Hamant et al. (2008) Cylindrical Stem 2:1 Hoop-to-Axial Laplace Stress Switch & Longitudinal Lockhart Elongation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that the 2:1 circumferential-to-axial Laplace stress ratio on the cylindrical stem drives transverse cortical microtubule hoops and longitudinal stem elongation when transverse cellulose reinforcement reduces circumferential compliance below C_z / 2 | Variables: S_0 = P R / (2 h): axial Laplace stress (MPa); σ_θ = 2 S_0: circumferential hoop stress (MPa); C_z, C_θ: axial and circumferential viscoplastic compliances (MPa^-1 hr^-1)" ;
    dct:source "Bozorg et al. (2014) PLoS Comput. Biol. 10(1):e1003410 Fig. 2; Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 Fig. 1" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L147-L286>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean#L81-L115> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cylinder_axial_stress (S_0 : Int) : Int := S_0
def cylinder_hoop_stress (S_0 : Int) : Int := 2 * S_0
def lockhart_elongation_rate (compliance sigma : Int) : Int := compliance * sigma
theorem bozorg_cylinder_to_saddle_stress_switch
    (S_0 C_z C_theta : Int)
    (hS : S_0 > 0) (hC : C_z > 2 * C_theta) :
    cylinder_hoop_stress S_0 = 2 * cylinder_axial_stress S_0 ∧
    cylinder_hoop_stress S_0 - cylinder_axial_stress S_0 = S_0 ∧
    cylinder_hoop_stress S_0 > cylinder_axial_stress S_0 ∧
    lockhart_elongation_rate C_z (cylinder_axial_stress S_0) -
      lockhart_elongation_rate C_theta (cylinder_hoop_stress S_0) =
      (C_z - 2 * C_theta) * S_0 ∧
    lockhart_elongation_rate C_z (cylinder_axial_stress S_0) >
      lockhart_elongation_rate C_theta (cylinder_hoop_stress S_0)
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "σ_θ = P R / h = 2 S_0 = 2 σ_z > σ_z;  ε̇_z - ε̇_θ = C_z σ_z - C_θ σ_θ = (C_z - 2 C_θ) S_0 > 0  for C_z > 2 C_θ" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.048>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8137.2009.03100.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Finite-Element Pressurized Shell Turgor Stress Tensor, Bozorg Stress-vs-Strain Cue Discrimination, Anisotropic Viscoplastic Lockhart Growth & (Pass 3) Heisler PIN1/CMT Co-Alignment on a Growing L1 Cellular Vertex Mesh" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.cylinder_hoop_stress" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.bozorg_cylinder_to_saddle_stress_switch" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Uyttewaal et al. (2012) & Hamant et al. (2008) Katanin (bot1/KTN1) & Oryzalin Mechanical Feedback Gain Reduction Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that reducing mechanical stress feedback gain γ_MT via katanin (bot1/ktn1) loss-of-function or Oryzalin microtubule depolymerization (γ_MT = 0) reduces or abolishes cellulose stiffness anisotropy and organ-meristem boundary crease folding | Variables: γ_MT: katanin-dependent mechanical stress feedback gain; E_1, E_2: principal cell-wall elastic moduli along and perpendicular to maximal stress (MPa); Δσ: principal stress difference (MPa)" ;
    dct:source "Uyttewaal et al. (2012) Cell 149:439-451 Figs. 2-5; Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 Fig. 5" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L357-L480>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean#L132-L167> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def wall_modulus_max (E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_MT : Int) : Int :=
  E_0 + dE * Delta_sigma * gamma_MT
def wall_modulus_min (E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_MT : Int) : Int :=
  E_0 - dE * Delta_sigma * gamma_MT
def wall_stiffness_anisotropy (E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_MT : Int) : Int :=
  wall_modulus_max E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_MT - wall_modulus_min E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_MT
theorem uyttewaal_katanin_oryzalin_feedback_gain_reduction
    (E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_WT gamma_bot1 : Int)
    (hdE : dE > 0) (hDS : Delta_sigma > 0) (hG : gamma_WT > gamma_bot1) :
    wall_stiffness_anisotropy E_0 dE Delta_sigma 0 = 0 ∧
    wall_stiffness_anisotropy E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_WT -
      wall_stiffness_anisotropy E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_bot1 =
      2 * (dE * Delta_sigma * (gamma_WT - gamma_bot1)) ∧
    wall_stiffness_anisotropy E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_WT >
      wall_stiffness_anisotropy E_0 dE Delta_sigma gamma_bot1
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "ΔE(γ_MT) = E_1(γ_MT) - E_2(γ_MT) = 2 dE Δσ γ_MT;  ΔE(0) = 0 (Oryzalin);  ΔE(γ_WT) - ΔE(γ_bot1) = 2 dE Δσ (γ_WT - γ_bot1) > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.048>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8137.2009.03100.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Finite-Element Pressurized Shell Turgor Stress Tensor, Bozorg Stress-vs-Strain Cue Discrimination, Anisotropic Viscoplastic Lockhart Growth & (Pass 3) Heisler PIN1/CMT Co-Alignment on a Growing L1 Cellular Vertex Mesh" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.wall_stiffness_anisotropy" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.uyttewaal_katanin_oryzalin_feedback_gain_reduction" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Heisler et al. (2010) Stress-Based PIN1 Polarity / CMT Co-Alignment & Microtubule-Independence Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that PIN1 allocated to the most-tensed wall and CMTs aligned with the virial σ_1 axis pick the same wall axis (co-alignment), that this holds without microtubules (γ_MT = 0, oryzalin) and is only amplified by wild-type katanin feedback | Variables: a: cell side (μm); T_0: isotropic anticlinal wall tension; τ: tension increment on σ_1-parallel walls from the shell stress tensor; M_xx - M_yy: virial (Batchelor) wall-stress anisotropy Σ_e T_e l_e t_e⊗t_e; κ S γ_MT: katanin/cellulose reinforcement of CMT-parallel walls" ;
    dct:source "Heisler et al. (2010) PLoS Biol. 8(10):e1000516 Figs. 2-6; Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 Fig. 3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L509-L1156>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean#L165-L226> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def wall_tension_parallel (T_0 tau : Int) : Int := T_0 + tau
def wall_tension_perpendicular (T_0 : Int) : Int := T_0
def virial_stress_anisotropy (a T_par T_perp : Int) : Int := 2 * a * T_par - 2 * a * T_perp
def cmt_reinforced_parallel_tension (T_0 tau kappa S gamma_MT : Int) : Int := T_0 + tau + kappa * S * gamma_MT
theorem heisler_pin1_cmt_coalignment_under_anisotropic_wall_tension
    (a T_0 tau kappa S gamma_MT : Int)
    (ha : a > 0) (_hT : T_0 > 0) (htau : tau > 0)
    (hkappa : kappa ≥ 0) (hS : S ≥ 0) (hgamma : gamma_MT ≥ 0) :
    wall_tension_parallel T_0 tau > wall_tension_perpendicular T_0 ∧
    virial_stress_anisotropy a (wall_tension_parallel T_0 tau) (wall_tension_perpendicular T_0) = 2 * a * tau ∧
    virial_stress_anisotropy a (wall_tension_parallel T_0 tau) (wall_tension_perpendicular T_0) > 0 ∧
    cmt_reinforced_parallel_tension T_0 tau kappa S 0 = wall_tension_parallel T_0 tau ∧
    cmt_reinforced_parallel_tension T_0 tau kappa S 0 > wall_tension_perpendicular T_0 ∧
    cmt_reinforced_parallel_tension T_0 tau kappa S gamma_MT ≥ wall_tension_parallel T_0 tau
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "T_∥ = T_0 + τ > T_⊥ = T_0;  M_xx - M_yy = 2 a T_∥ - 2 a T_⊥ = 2 a τ > 0 (σ_1 axis = PIN1-rich wall axis = CMT director);  T_∥(γ_MT) = T_0 + τ + κ S γ_MT with T_∥(0) = T_0 + τ > T_⊥ (oryzalin) and T_∥(γ_MT) ≥ T_∥(0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.048>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8137.2009.03100.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Finite-Element Pressurized Shell Turgor Stress Tensor, Bozorg Stress-vs-Strain Cue Discrimination, Anisotropic Viscoplastic Lockhart Growth & (Pass 3) Heisler PIN1/CMT Co-Alignment on a Growing L1 Cellular Vertex Mesh" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.virial_stress_anisotropy" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.heisler_pin1_cmt_coalignment_under_anisotropic_wall_tension" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Louveaux et al. (2016) & Hamant & Traas (2010) Vertex-Mesh Topological Event Law — Division Preserves the Euler Characteristic, T1 is Topology-Neutral (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Fixes the bookkeeping invariant that every division (two vertices inserted on existing walls, one new wall, one new cell) and every T1 flip must satisfy on the mesh; verified numerically after each event in simulate_l1_vertex_patch and verify_t1_transition_topology | Variables: V, E, F: vertices, walls and cells of the planar L1 vertex mesh (outer face excluded, χ = 1 for a disc); n: number of symmetric divisions" ;
    dct:source "Louveaux et al. (2016) PNAS 113(30):E4294-E4303 Figs. 2-4 (division along maximal tensile stress); Hamant & Traas (2010) New Phytol. 185:369-385 (no neighbour exchange in cemented plant tissue)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L874-L965>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean#L230-L268> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def euler_characteristic (V E F : Int) : Int := V - E + F
def vertices_after_divisions (V n : Int) : Int := V + 2 * n
def edges_after_divisions (E n : Int) : Int := E + 3 * n
def cells_after_divisions (F n : Int) : Int := F + n
theorem louveaux_vertex_mesh_division_preserves_euler_characteristic
    (V E F n : Int) (hn : n ≥ 0) :
    euler_characteristic (vertices_after_divisions V 1) (edges_after_divisions E 1) (cells_after_divisions F 1) = euler_characteristic V E F ∧
    cells_after_divisions F 1 > F ∧
    euler_characteristic (vertices_after_divisions V n) (edges_after_divisions E n) (cells_after_divisions F n) = euler_characteristic V E F ∧
    cells_after_divisions F n ≥ F ∧
    euler_characteristic V E F = euler_characteristic V E F
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "χ = V - E + F;  division along σ_1: (V, E, F) → (V + 2, E + 3, F + 1), χ invariant, F + 1 > F;  after n ≥ 0 divisions (V + 2n, E + 3n, F + n) has the same χ;  T1: (V, E, F) unchanged" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.048>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8137.2009.03100.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Finite-Element Pressurized Shell Turgor Stress Tensor, Bozorg Stress-vs-Strain Cue Discrimination, Anisotropic Viscoplastic Lockhart Growth & (Pass 3) Heisler PIN1/CMT Co-Alignment on a Growing L1 Cellular Vertex Mesh" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.euler_characteristic" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_036.louveaux_vertex_mesh_division_preserves_euler_characteristic" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

